 "sections": [
  {
   "heading": "(页面开头)",
   "blocks": [
    {
     "kind": "p",
     "text": "All ships in nebulous are covered with a layer of armor. In order to damage components, the attack must first penetrate armor. Armor in neb can be degraded in specific areas by attacks, both penetrating and nonpenetrating. In specific terms: Armor health is stored as a texture mask layered across that takes localized damage only where it is hit. Armor is layered across the hull equally, protecting turrets, radar panels, and thrusters to the same degree as everything else."
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "heading": "Guidelines",
   "blocks": [
    {
     "kind": "p",
     "text": "Ammo selection for a given targets can be accomplished visually in several steps"
    },
    {
     "kind": "li",
     "depth": 1,
     "text": "Start by shooting with AP"
    },
    {
     "kind": "li",
     "depth": 1,
     "text": "If you’re shooting AP, and your shells punch out the back of the target, switch to HE."
    },
    {
     "kind": "li",
     "depth": 1,
     "text": "If you’re shooting HE, and you see showers of sparks for ricochets, switch to AP."
    },
    {
     "kind": "li",
     "depth": 1,
     "text": "If you’re firing at a small target, fire RPF/Bombshell/Grape until it stops evading, then HE to destroy"
    },
    {
     "kind": "p",
     "text": "Key: X -> Y = “shoot X to damage, then finish with Y” X or Y = “use X, but Y has situational uses”. Lack of bolding indicates either works X :-( = “your best option, but alas, it won’t do much”"
