  {
   "heading": "Mechanics",
   "blocks": []
  },
  {
   "heading": "Mechanics › Armor Damage",
   "blocks": []
  },
  {
   "heading": "Mechanics › Armor Damage › Terminology",
   "blocks": [
    {
     "kind": "li",
     "depth": 0,
     "text": "Nominal armor (NA)"
    },
    {
     "kind": "li",
     "depth": 0,
     "text": "NA is the actual thickness of the armor as listed in the hull description."
    },
    {
     "kind": "li",
     "depth": 0,
     "text": "Effective armor (EA)"
    },
    {
     "kind": "li",
     "depth": 0,
     "text": "EA is based on the angle of the armor relative to the incoming projectile, increased from NA due to the projectile having to travel through more armor. This is capped at 2.5x nominal armor."
    },
    {
     "kind": "li",
     "depth": 0,
     "text": "[math]\\displaystyle{ \\text{EA} = \\min\\left(\\frac{\\text{NA}}{\\cos\\theta}\\, ,\\, 2.5\\times\\text{NA}\\right) }[/math]"
    },
    {
     "kind": "li",
     "depth": 0,
     "text": "where [math]\\displaystyle{ \\theta }[/math] is the angle from the normal to the incoming projectile."
    },
    {
     "kind": "li",
     "depth": 0,
     "text": "Some weapons ignore armor angling, so for these EA simply equals NA."
    },
    {
     "kind": "li",
     "depth": 0,
     "text": "Remaining armor (RA)"
    },
    {
     "kind": "li",
     "depth": 0,
     "text": "RA is the remaining effective armor, i.e. EA times the current armor health in that location."
    },
    {
     "kind": "li",
     "depth": 0,
     "text": "[math]\\displaystyle{ \\text{RA} = \\text{current armor health fraction}\\times\\text{EA} }[/math]"
    },
    {
     "kind": "li",
     "depth": 0,
     "text": "Armor Penetration (AP)"
    },
    {
     "kind": "li",
     "depth": 0,
     "text": "AP is the base penetration stat of the weapon."
    },
    {
     "kind": "p",
     "text": "If [math]\\displaystyle{ \\text{AP} \\geq \\text{RA} }[/math] then the attack penetrates and shreds all the armor at that location. If not, then the armor is damaged according to the process below."
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "heading": "Mechanics › Armor Damage › Ricochet",
   "blocks": [
    {
     "kind": "p",
     "text": "Shells can ricochet off of armor at steep angles with reduced shredding and a visual effect."
    },
    {
     "kind": "p",
     "text": "If a shell does not have the AP to penetrate, it will ricochet if the angle to the normal is greater than 80 degrees:"
    },
    {
     "kind": "p",
     "text": "[math]\\displaystyle{ \\text{ricochet if}\\quad \\theta\\geq 80^\\circ }[/math] Ignoring armor angling does not by itself prevent a ricochet: the ricochet test still uses the real impact angle. Missiles, rockets, mines, bombs and beams never ricochet because they set NeverRicochet. Plasma ignores angling for thickness and can still ricochet.[1]"
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "heading": "Mechanics › Armor Damage › Damage Formula",
   "blocks": [
    {
     "kind": "p",
     "text": "For shells that do not ignore armor angling, AP is modified based on the impact angle and amount of armor remaining. Simply, AP is scaled by the fraction of itself over RA."
    },
    {
     "kind": "p",
     "text": "Putting it all together, the actual shredding applied to the armor is"
    },
    {
     "kind": "p",
     "text": "[math]\\displaystyle{ \\text{actualDamage} = \\text{AP}\\times\\rho\\times\\min\\left(\\frac{\\text{AP}}{\\text{RA}}\\, ,\\, 1\\right) }[/math]"
    },
    {
     "kind": "li",
     "depth": 0,
     "text": "where [math]\\displaystyle{ \\rho }[/math] is 0.2 if the shot ricochets or 1 if it does not. Then [math]\\displaystyle{ \\text{actualDamage} }[/math] is shredded from the armor in a rough circle across the armor shredding radius centered at the point of impact."
    },
    {
     "kind": "p",
     "text": "For example, a 120mm AP Shell strikes a Solomon at at 30 degree angle from the normal."
    },
    {
     "kind": "li",
     "depth": 1,
     "text": "AP = 45 cm."
    },
    {
     "kind": "li",
     "depth": 1,
     "text": "EA = NA / cos(30) = 64.7 cm."
    },
    {
     "kind": "li",
     "depth": 1,
     "text": "RA = EA (because this Solomon has not taken any hits there)"
    },
    {
     "kind": "li",
     "depth": 1,
     "text": "Does not ricochet."
    },
    {
     "kind": "p",
     "text": "Then the actualDamage done is [math]\\displaystyle{ \\text{actualDamage} = 45 \\times \\frac{45}{64.7} = 31.3\\, \\text{cm} }[/math]. So the Solomon would have 24.7 cm of armor remaining in that spot."
    },
    {
     "kind": "li",
     "depth": 1,
     "text": "Note that even if armor is reduced to zero, the attack will not penetrate unless the earlier [math]\\displaystyle{ \\text{AP} \\geq \\text{RA} }[/math] condition is fulfilled. This generally happens at steeper angles, eg 60cm pen vs 56cm armor at 30 degrees will not penetrate, but will fully strip armor.[needs confirmation]"
    },
    {
     "kind": "li",
     "depth": 1,
     "text": "Some damage types such as HEI warheads (missiles, rockets, mines), and Plasma ignore armor angle and will strip listed penetration regardless of angle. Beams never ricochet but still use effective armor thickness (nominal thickness divided by cos θ, capped at 2.5× nominal), so angled hits shred armor more slowly than perpendicular hits. [2]"
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "heading": "Mechanics › Armor Damage Radius",
   "blocks": [
    {
     "kind": "p",
     "text": "The damage from the equations above are applied to the mask with a brushsize roughly equal to the armor damage radius. This shredding radius is not listed in game but can be viewed in the specific Munitions & Missiles page."
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "heading": "Mechanics › Overpenetration",
   "blocks": [
    {
     "kind": "p",
     "text": "Further information: component damage: overpenetration"
    },
    {
     "kind": "p",
     "text": "If a shell is able to penetrate and does not stop inside the hull, it makes another check to penetrate the armor on the other side to exit the hull. The armor penetration is reduced by the distance traveled through the ship's interior density[needs confirmation]. If the second penetration check succeeds, the round overpenetrates and does reduced damage."
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "heading": "Notes",
   "blocks": [
    {
     "kind": "li",
     "depth": 1,
     "text": "↑ Plasma can still ricochet. If it fails to penetrate at 80 degrees or more, it shreds 20% and applies no heat, and it does not go on to damage components"
    },
    {
     "kind": "li",
     "depth": 1,
     "text": "↑ Damage types ignoring angling appears to be a property of the damage type rather than a serializable field in most cases."
    }
   ]
  },
